  {
   "id": "e44",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 450,
   "width": 767.2500000000001,
   "height": 112.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#000000",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 417193478,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1004106764,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1. CPU 2 has no oven tasks, so balance_oven() runs before picking the next task\n2. find busiest CPU with >= 2 oven tasks (lockless read)  ->  CPU 0 (4 tasks)\n3. double_lock_balance(CPU 2, CPU 0): fixed lock order, no deadlock; recheck both counts\n4. skip the running task; take first task allowed on CPU 2  ->  fib35 (lowest waiting weight)\n5. move_queued_task_locked(): fib35 now runs on CPU 2\nLower weight = shorter job = earlier in queue (SJF)",
   "originalText": "1. CPU 2 has no oven tasks, so balance_oven() runs before picking the next task\n2. find busiest CPU with >= 2 oven tasks (lockless read)  ->  CPU 0 (4 tasks)\n3. double_lock_balance(CPU 2, CPU 0): fixed lock order, no deadlock; recheck both counts\n4. skip the running task; take first task allowed on CPU 2  ->  fib35 (lowest waiting weight)\n5. move_queued_task_locked(): fib35 now runs on CPU 2\nLower weight = shorter job = earlier in queue (SJF)",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  }
